# Full judgment text, 321KB of it, retrieved through an Internet Archive
# snapshot of BAILII. It is ignored rather than merely uncommitted because
# src/routes/Cases.jsx tells readers on screen that this app does not reproduce
# judgments — committing this file would make the app's own statement to its
# readers false, which is worse than the copying. Two commits tonight swept
# files nobody intended via a broad `git add`, so the exclusion is written down
# rather than left to whoever runs the next one.
#
# Nothing imports it; excluding it costs the app nothing. If the tier is ever
# revived, the honest form is the one the extracts already use: a citation, the
# free source, and what to look for.
content/judgments/
